WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.590
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.650
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.490
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.490
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.420
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:59.260
<b>In the second half of this episode, we enter the "What Story Is This?" arc...</b>

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.380
Excuse me!

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.770
Hello! Welcome to the Adventurers' Guild!

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.800
Well, well.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.340
Good to see you, Alvin-san.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.170
It's been a while.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.580
You're looking well, too, Carla-san.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.200
C'mon, say hello like a functional person!

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:15.060
Can you please not talk 
to me as if we're frie—

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.410
Okay! That's quite enough!

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.580
Apologies for my little goblin here.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.090
N-Not at all.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.320
I'm glad to see her as energetic as ever.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.580
Now, how can I help you today?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.180
I'm here to review my adventurer rank.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.620
Review your rank?

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.860
You're not thinking "he doesn't really think 
it's gone up? LOL-in-parentheses!" are you?

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:37.520
That's so rude!

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.060
That's what <i>you're</i> thinking!

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.770
Actually, I was thinking "I really hope his 
rank hasn't gone down! LOL-in-parentheses."

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:44.940
It's very different!

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.290
Well, keep it to yourself!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.910
In this case, please apply your 
blood seal to this rank testing sheet.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.920
The magic circle drawn on it will offer 
you a rank from one star to five stars

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.900
based on your accomplishments 
and experiences.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.490
A blood seal?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.410
Are you sure about that, Alvin-san?

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.300
It's just a little prick on the fingertip.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.780
What are you so worried about?

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.910
I thought you might die from blood loss...

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.410
Like hell!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.250
You need a little help with that?

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.030
You mean the healing part, right?

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.760
Come to think of it, Alvin-san. 
What is your current ranking?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.100
Oh, sorry. I'm sure it's one star—

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:22.720
Zero.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.080
Last time, the magic circle 
didn't react at all.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.030
Which means my rank is zero stars.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.180
Funny, isn't it?

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.430
I'm sorry.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.110
It didn't occur to me that your rank 
might not be able to get any lower.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.190
By the way, what's your rank, Carla?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.350
Well... three stars, actually.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.750
I see.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.570
But I'm sure that with your stars, there were 
just too many dark clouds to see them...

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.160
Because they're stars... get it?

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.880
"Too many dark clouds" is more 
like the story of my life.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.420
<i>Really not funny...</i>

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.990
Funny, right?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.320
I'm sure it was just a 
defective testing sheet.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.370
That's it!

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.670
I'm sure you just got 
unlucky with the device!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.710
Five times in a row?

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:11.440
Y-Yes, five defective sheets!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.930
Poor Alvin-san! No luck at all!

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.010
Or "no rank at all," I guess I should say...

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:17.930
You know?

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.610
It's just a joke, Alvin-san!

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.290
I was trying to lighten the mood!

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.910
Calm down!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.460
Throwing in more blood 
won't make a difference,

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:32.830
so please don't do anything 
we'll both regret!

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.420
I'm sure you'll get stars this time,

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.080
even without offering up your worthless arm!

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.240
You've survived encounters 
with all kinds of monsters.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.600
The golem, the cyclops, the 
necromancer... even the Medusa!

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.590
Really?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.720
You survived battles with all 
of those savage monsters?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.570
Well... that technically 
describes it, but...

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:56.680
I'm sure you'll get one star—
no, you could even get four!

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.430
You think?

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.940
Isn't that great?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.850
You'll be propelled into the 
ranks of the adventuring elite!

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.050
Well, well... We don't know 
that for sure, just yet.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:07.700
But it is true.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.340
I have had experiences that 
most adventurers haven't.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.710
I think I've been doing pretty 
good, relatively speaking!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.450
Can we skip past the small 
talk and get to the testing?

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.400
C'mon, don't rush me!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.800
Boy, might be about time 
to figure out my title!

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:24.720
You know?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.620
How many stars will I get?

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.970
Look, Alvin-san! It's changing!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.110
You've got at least one star!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.230
<b>(LOL)</b>

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.230
LOL-in-parentheses.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.340
I told you, it doesn't matter 
how much blood you use!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.280
You could have picked a 
better way to stop me!

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.280
What's this?

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.690
I thought I heard a commotion 
in here. If it isn't Alvin!

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.340
What a surprise...

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.300
That you're still alive, that is.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.820
I figured you'd died to 
some stray dog's bite.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.320
You know him?

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.170
Yeah... he's an adventurer, just like us.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.460
Just like you?

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.860
Don't make me laugh!

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:17.510
A pathetic weenie like you doesn't 
belong in the same category as me!

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.860
What did he just say?

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.640
Let it go. It's just a cheap provocation.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:27.150
Did you just call Alvin-san a lousy, stinking, 
slug weenie loser nothing old man?!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.330
How dare you?!

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.680
He didn't say most of that!

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.670
Who in the world is this guy who 
looks like an escaped felon?

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:33.790
Escaped felon?!

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.060
You're a funny little kid...

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.820
Mind telling me your name?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.420
Don't you know it's basic manners to give 
your name before asking for someone else's?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.660
Oh, wait! You don't want to give your 
name because you're on the run!

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.050
You little brat...

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.780
Calm down, Brigan!

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:55.120
She doesn't mean any harm! 
She just doesn't have a filter, that's all!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.540
Brigan. I see.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.680
I truly apologize for my little goblin!

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.420
Is that your name?

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.290
That's a very nice name.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.380
Yes, yes...

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.280
See? That's also how she feels!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.130
It sounds like "prison."

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.520
Perfect for an escaped convict.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.770
You didn't have to say that!

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.370
You lousy, little dark elf...

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.860
Give it a rest—

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.840
A dark elf, dressed as a healer...

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.420
The irritating behavior...

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.670
You're not "Carla," are you?

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.540
Indeed I am!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.610
Carla, also known as the goddess 
who descended from the heavens!

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:27.500
Smug face!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.380
<i>I wish you could have descended 
straight to the underworld...</i>

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.330
You two have formed a party, then, have you?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.760
Well... there were circumstances.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:44.050
The infamous disaster 
land mine healer Carla,

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:48.300
and "the walking load" Alvin, 
in a party together?

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.950
This is too priceless!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.530
H-How dare you?!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.390
Did you hear what he said to us, Alvin-san?

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.060
Doesn't it frustrate you?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.290
But I can't exactly say he's wrong...

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.450
He called me the "disaster land mine healer"!

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.760
Doesn't it frustrate you?

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.040
Oh, that part? Not at all.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.670
It frustrates me.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.430
To hear him call you "the walking load"...

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.340
Carla...

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.030
You don't just walk! You talk, too!

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.340
Speaking of, I could do with 
a lot less talking from you!

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.850
C'mon, that was a compliment.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.770
A pain in the ass elf and 
a human ball and chain.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.910
You're a perfect match!

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.720
A p-perfect match?

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.240
Gosh, I wouldn't say that...

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:29.900
Right?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.220
Pure slander.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.750
Why don't we call ourselves "Team Exile"?

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:35.940
I hate that too much!

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.750
And why are you enjoying this?!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.710
Exile! I love it!

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.600
You've got good taste!

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:43.740
Right? Right?

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:47.860
Though, Brigan-san, 
you deserve the title "Ex-Con."

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.550
You little brat!

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:57.560
H-He's mad for no reason!

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:58.910
What a low boiling point!

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:00.350
<i>Not</i> for no reason!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.780
I'm impressed he lasted as long as he did!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.430
What do you take me for?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.410
Guess I'll have to teach 
you a painful lesson!

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.410
Hey, Alvin!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.450
Let me at her—

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.780
But I refuse!

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:14.540
I'm not such a coward as to sit back and 
take all the abuse you've dished out, either.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.780
Alvin-san...

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.340
What, you wanna fight?

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.910
Sounds good to me!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.110
Let's step outside!

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.880
Wh-What will we do?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.240
Accept the challenge.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.370
I have my own form of pride!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.280
But he's probably going 
beat the shit out of me,

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.000
so could I get some healing afterwards?

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.500
Sure thing!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.970
Hey, what's wrong?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.380
Are you coming or not, you filthy coward?

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.510
Shut up!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.010
I'm on my way! Just you wait!

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:41.500
Don't run away!

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.190
Please. I've been waiting for this!

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:45.600
You're open!

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.780
B-Brigan!

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:53.110
What did you do?!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:56.650
Well, he was wide open...

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.100
I thought he was asking for it.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.880
Are you an assassin now?!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.740
<b>The legendary
pro wrestler
The Cuban
Assassin
#1</b>

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.740
m 0 0 l 15 0 l 15 20 l 0 20

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.740
<b>Special Moves:</b>

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.740
<b>Any rule-breaking
attack</b>

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.080
Not that!

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.490
<b>Special Moves:</b>

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.490
<b>Any surprise
attack</b>

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.490
Yes, more like that!

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.860
Thank goodness! He's alive!

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.660
Wh-What just happened?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.850
Well, actually... I'm sorry...

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.930
No, maybe we should treat them first?

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.170
This is where I step in.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.800
Why are you tying him up?!

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.550
Got him in custody!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.060
He's seriously not an escaped felon!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.260
Is this the mansion in question?

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.380
Yes.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.730
The mansion in which the evil spirit dwells.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.530
We have to exorcise it, right?

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:39.460
Yes...

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:42.580
We destroyed a table in 
that fight with Brigan,

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:44.580
and made a lot of trouble for the Guild.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.780
So this is our punishment.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.400
It looks like an ordinary 
old ruin at a glance,

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.280
but I detect a terrifying aura from it.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:55.450
I hear it's known as the 
"Shocking Rocking Horror House!"

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.910
Suddenly, it sounds like an attraction.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:04.940
But the rumors say that anyone who 
enters this mansion never comes out alive.

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:09.760
It's believed that they're killed by 
the evil spirit that dwells within.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:13.240
There it is! 
The classic horror house setup line!

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.670
It's always made up! Don't tell me you 
actually believe, etcetera, etcetera.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.510
You mean you don't believe in it?

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:21.320
Is there anyone who actually 
believes stories like that?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>Ack</i>chyuwally...

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.870
I invited a special guest 
along to attest to just that.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:31.510
This person infiltrated 
the mansion once before.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:34.930
You can't do that! The setup is supposed 
to be that no one leaves there alive!

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.040
Show yourself!

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.910
Oh, hello there!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.410
Well, that's freaking haunted!

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:44.270
This is Anna-san, a former thief 
who infiltrated the mansion

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.480
and was tragically killed 
by the evil spirit there.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:47.450
Let's give her a hand!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.450
P-Please don't, Carla-chan!

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.600
It's embarrassing!

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.500
But I need to give you 
a proper introduction.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.300
But if you say I was "tragically killed," 
it makes me sound like a bad thief!

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.260
But you did die, so...

00:11:58.260 --> 00:11:59.270
It's not like that!

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.420
That evil spirit was really, really tough!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.910
Pad it with small talk!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.910
What the heck is he doing?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.550
Wait, are you still here?!

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:05.880
Where have you been?

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:10.870
Well, I was looking for Big Sis Carla's 
crystal ball, and I got lost...

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:13.390
We wrapped up that nonsense 
a while back, actually.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.200
What?

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.930
Well, I'd rather not stand 
outside talking forever.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.850
Let's go into the mansion 
and discuss it in there.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.570
It is awfully cold today...

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.360
The chill of the grave, right?

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.130
Wait, wait, wait!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.130
What?

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:28.280
We were going to go into the mansion,

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.170
roll some dice with subjects written on them,

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:32.530
and have a nice talk based on 
the outcome of the roll...

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:34.710
Happy! Rappy! Exciting talk!

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:35.780
Just shut up!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.770
What, you want to be part 
of our girls' talk?

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.290
As a man in his thirties, 
would you be able to contribute?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.120
How did you know how old I—

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.100
But never mind that!

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.420
The mansion is dangerous, right?

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.790
Why are you trying to go 
in like it's nothing?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.510
We need to hear what she has to 
say, figure out a plan, and—

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:54.270
Oho? Don't tell me...

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.590
Aw, no way!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.080
What?

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.410
It's not like I'm afraid or—

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:01.460
Oho!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.920
Just say it outright!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.800
And just so we're clear, 
I'm not afraid at all!

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:06.440
I mean it!

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.470
Don't be ashamed!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.830
Everyone has things they're afraid of.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.930
And evil spirits are like 
a reminder of death!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:16.320
Death is a fear that all 
living beings share!

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:18.390
I told you, I'm not scared!

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.270
But here's a question: Da-dun!

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.780
Who's the holy woman that evil spirits fear,

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:29.790
with divine protection, a vulnerable gaze that 
inflames the protective instincts of others,

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.440
silver hair, dark skin, 
and an altogether enchanting visage?

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.810
Correct!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.470
What in the world are you talking about?

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.150
Well, we have our plan to 
deal with the evil spirit.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:58.610
Let's go exorcise the thing!

00:13:58.610 --> 00:13:59.890
Yeah!

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:01.260
H-Hey!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.170
What's wrong!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.460
There is nothing to be afraid of.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.030
<i>You're</i> the thing I'm afraid of!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.790
It's fine.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.870
You have me, and I have a divine protection.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.710
Besides, the evil spirit might 
be willing to listen to reason.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:20.970
And even if it's not willing 
to listen to reason,

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:24.970
I can pound reason into it using 
my iron fists of brotherly love!

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.550
How in the world do you get 
"fists of brotherly love"?

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:33.930
Welcome ho—

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.950
I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm an 
absolutely worthless trash healer.

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.850
I am truly grateful you would form 
a party with one as worthless as I.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.430
At the same time, I am 
extremely filled with guilt.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:44.430
Crap! She's gone crazy from the fear, 
and she's actually talking sense!

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:49.430
I'm so obnoxious and worthless I should just 
go home and live as a shut-in forever.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.800
Hey. Don't talk like that!

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.710
It's okay. I'll forgive you for everything 
that's happened between us.

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.700
So please, stay exactly as you are now!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.230
I'm begging you!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:14:59.960
<b>Sincere</b>

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:03.720
What a generous thing to say!

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.770
The kindness to accept the 
faults of anyone around you...

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:06.450
You sound almost like...

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.300
Like me!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.930
Damn it! She's back!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.840
That's better.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.870
I didn't expect it to be that intense.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.400
I agree.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.100
An aura of hostility so powerful, 
it shakes even <i>me</i>...

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.940
Clearly, this is not an enemy we can 
deal with through normal means.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.600
But...

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:31.870
A new sacrifice has 
resulted from my failure!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.420
This is pretty tough.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:38.040
But can't you use a resurrection 
spell on the evil spirit?

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:42.490
You magic-ignorant bumpkins 
are so troubling sometimes.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.550
Resurrection is an extremely 
high-level spell.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.590
It's not something I can 
simply use on command!

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.340
Of course, I <i>can</i> use it...

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.520
You can?

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.320
But I still have a long way to go.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:58.020
I can only resurrect someone who's 
been dead three seconds or fewer.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.580
Three seconds?

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.730
Well, I guess it's better 
than not having it at all...

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.880
However...

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.770
the time it takes to cast 
the resurrection spell...

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.080
is... dun-dun-dun! Ten seconds!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.270
You won't make it in time!

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.900
But if I start thinking you might die, 
I can start the incantation in advance.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:17.030
So you might cast it before I die?

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.940
Well, never mind.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.570
Let's just get out of here.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:22.630
Could you please wait just a minute?

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:23.900
What is it?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.210
That evil spirit said something, didn't it?

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.680
I do think it tried to say "welcome home."

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.810
That's right.

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.010
What about it?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.510
It just seemed awfully presumptuous 
of it. I mean, we'd just met!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.380
Are you seriously...

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:40.990
Plus, I'm supposed to be an 
entity that evil spirits fear.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:45.390
So having that thing say "welcome home☆" as 
it escorts me inside feels kind of insulting.

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:47.320
I don't think it was quite that friendly...

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:49.530
This has never happened before.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:52.780
I've never had an evil spirit show 
such a lack of respect before.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.330
I'm not the kind of girl who 
can take this lying down!

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.740
I'm going to put that evil spirit 
in a catgirl maid outfit,

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.720
and make it say "welcome home, mew☆!"

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.160
That doesn't seem like 
much of a punishment...

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.340
Don't worry.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:07.300
I won't be rough with it.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.300
I'm just going to put it 
in a catgirl maid outfit.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.290
I've forgotten why we came 
here in the first place.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:14.740
Allow me tieshankao!

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:16.260
Do you have to open it like that?!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.930
Now, show yourself!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.810
I'll teach you proper manners for someone 
you're meeting for the first time!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.050
I don't want to hear that from someone 
who doesn't know how to open a door...

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.800
I-It's here, isn't it?!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:33.390
Y-You certainly humiliated me before!

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:36.360
But this time, you won't 
find it so easy-peasy!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.910
Open your eyes! Don't point at me!

00:17:39.190 --> 00:17:40.030
Carla!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.110
Wh-What now?!

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:42.490
Are you trying to scare me?

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.840
Just look behind you!

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.780
You can't scare me again!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.790
But if you shout out "wah" or something...

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:50.170
Welcome home, mew!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.300
That's pushing it!

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:53.920
But isn't that nice?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.780
It looks like it's reasonable after all!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.880
It's completely wrong!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.140
Just completely wrong!

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:04.270
It's obvious your heart's not in it!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.960
It's not just a matter of appearance! 
It's a matter of dedication!

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:07.510
Right?

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:11.260
The minute she realizes it's reasonable, 
she starts walking all over it...

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:12.830
But that face!

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:16.740
What people want from maids 
these days is rejuvenation.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.620
What's with the holy woman pose?

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:21.030
A truly heartfelt desire to serve another

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:24.100
is more rejuvenating than any healing spell.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.190
It is, indeed, the ultimate rejuvenation!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:30.370
But merely putting on a maid outfit 
will not confer true rejuvenation!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.960
There are some healers who can't 
rejuvenate a damned thing, either.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.240
But...

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:42.220
Seeking rejuvenation from an evil spirit 
like you might be too high a bar...

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.560
All right. I know what to do!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.400
Just this one time, 
the rejuvenation specialist,

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.910
"rejuvelist" for short...

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:53.730
That's hard to say!

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.810
...will teach you the hidden 
secrets of rejuvenation!

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:57.610
For real?

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:00.270
It's going to be hard, violent training.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.870
Do you still wish to pursue it?

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:03.840
Please!

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.070
That was easy!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.620
<b>Push-ups x 100
Sit-ups x 200
Voice Training x 10 minutes
Squats 2 sets of 10</b>

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:10.660
<i>And so Carla unveiled her 
intense training regimen.</i>

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.000
<b>Carla-chan  Awesome!! x 100</b>

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>She <i>unveiled</i> it, but she didn't 
actually put it into practice.</i>

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.380
Honestly, smiling's about 
all you need to do...

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.420
Right...

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.720
<i>Then she talked about
something-or-other for five minutes...</i>

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:22.860
<i>And then...</i>

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.900
All done! Yay!

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:29.510
It doesn't look any different...

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:31.770
Actually, it's gotten more twisted!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.520
Now, do just as I advised you!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.860
Advised her?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:36.890
Did you do that?

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.790
W... W...

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:46.580
W-W-Welcome home...

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:46.580
This doesn't seem good!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:49.110
Mew!

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:50.860
No freakin' way!

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:52.580
Wait, wait!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.580
Who the hell is that?

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:56.560
Who is it? What's wrong with you?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.040
It's the evil spirit!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.090
She's been here the whole time!

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.080
Has not!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:03.730
That's obviously a different life form!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.720
<b>After</b>

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.720
<b>Before</b>

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.810
Life form? You old silly!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.590
She's totally dead!

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.590
That's not the point!

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:13.400
Well, I'm sure it's very surprising to you,

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.800
and I'm sure you want to 
shower me with praise...

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.100
And I really appreciate 
the round of applause...

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.860
But please, let's turn it down, 
and sit back down.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:23.100
Nobody's giving you a standing ovation!

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:26.580
Before I could pass on the 
secrets of rejuvenation,

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.660
I had to purify the heart of my successor!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.740
Hang on a minute.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:33.630
That means you couldn't 
possibly pass on any secrets!

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.270
Because your own heart is pitch black!

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.210
There, I win.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:42.790
As a result, the evil spirit 
was purified, inside and out.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:44.680
Hey, don't just ignore me.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.890
Earlier, too, we weren't just talking.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:51.460
I was letting her vent all her 
anger, stress, and worries.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.680
Are you a counselor now?

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:56.400
And I carefully plucked out the 
seeds of her anger and resentment.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.310
Do you have a per-episode 
quota for that pose?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.570
Yes, it's almost like...

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:03.560
the way the Grim Reaper plucks 
out the life of a living being.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:04.010
Right?

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:05.820
Not a great choice of words.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.530
Hang on a minute!

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.720
Oh, you're back to life?

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.430
Actually, I guess you're still dead...

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:12.600
Thank you for the help before.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.580
No, wait!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:17.320
She's pretty cute now that 
she's been purified, but...

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:22.080
Having two cute little ghosts 
around is just redundant!

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.670
Is that all you have to say 
to the being that killed you?

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.470
Wait just a mushroom!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:30.600
There's only room for one cute mascot 
on this team, and that's me!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.740
No one actually thinks of you that way...

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:33.820
Wait a minute!

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.860
The cute mascot on this 
team is obviously m—

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.860
I'm not letting you finish that one!

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:47.800
The real cutie on this team is m—

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:50.050
I'm not letting you say it!

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:27.040
Isn't that great, Ryoko-chan?

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.510
We've made our anime debut!

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:29.950
We have, Anna-san!

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:32.310
Especially since we don't appear 
in the official publication!

00:23:32.310 --> 00:23:35.570
But becoming regulars as of 
the next episode is like a dream!

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:37.810
Let's do our best 
to make the show exciting!

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>"So, this is Part 2 of the "What Story Is This?" arc and I'm really
glad we found out a way for Anna and Ryoko to get involved
and also to fill in some time based on the fact that there's not
enough manga material available but there's also a reference
to that classic family anime in this episode that I think a lot
of people will get even if I don't explain it but it's been a chance
to think about how animators back then had to put so much care
into drawing each cel by hand instead of doing it digitally like
we do now which is pretty cool and that's the deal with episode 11."</b>

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.410
Wait, there're only two more episodes!

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:40.150
Wh—
